  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 353 PM CDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nA weak cold front will come move southward from the \nnorthern Plains into northwest Sandhills by Sunday morning. \nDespite the advancing cold front will still see temperatures \nabove normal on Sunday, with the warmest temperatures across \nsouthwest Nebraska where the front will be slower to advance \nthrough, highs will reach the upper 80s. Across northern \nNebraska temperatures will only reach the low to mid 70s as the \nfront will pass through before peak heating. The front stalls \nout Monday, keeping one more day 80s across far southwest \nNebraska. As far as overnight lows on Sunday night and Monday \nnight, not expecting at this time to see any need for any \nfrost/freeze headlines, although overnight temps do cool \nconsiderably by Monday night, with temperatures in the low 40s, \nincreased cloudiness overnight will likely keep temperatures in \nthe low 40s or possibly see an increasing trend of overnight \nlows as cloud coverage looks to be expanding with latest model \nguidance due to some influence of tropical moisture from \nsouthwest. \n\nFrom mid-week til the end of the long term period, will see a cooler \nair mass settle in to the region and temperatures will cool to near \nnormal with highs in the 60s to low 70s. There will also be chances \nfor precipitation with increase moisture and weak disturbances on \nTuesday night through early Thursday.",
